# tokenAtlas - optional per-machine overrides. Copy to .env only if needed.
#
# Prefer setup and Settings on a new installation. Leave overrides unset until
# the archive and source folders are selected. OneDrive is optional.
#
# .env is gitignored - it describes this PC, not the project.

# --- Where the archive lives ------------------------------------------------
# The archive is the canonical ingest source: live vendor folders get pruned,
# the archive only ever gains files. Everything reads from it and _sync.bat
# mirrors into it.
#
# Use an explicit private folder when overriding the location selected in setup.
#
# TOKENATLAS_ARCHIVE=D:\AI-archive

# --- Local database and disposable working files ----------------------------
# Choose the database folder in Settings to copy and verify the existing index
# before restarting. Results and incremental progress must stay outside the
# source archive and cloud folders. The filename remains unchanged.
# TOKENATLAS_DB=C:\Users\you\.tokenatlas\atlas.sqlite
#
# Disposable work only: source SQLite backup preparation and database copying.
# Settings can select a folder without a restart; that machine-local selection
# takes precedence over this default. Recovery work and completed results are
# never stored here. Default: <local machine state>/temp.
# TOKENATLAS_TEMP_DIR=C:\Users\you\AppData\Local\tokenAtlas\temp

# --- Local Atlas index snapshots --------------------------------------------
# Recovery copies of atlas.sqlite stay beside the active local database by
# default (for example C:\Users\you\.tokenatlas\atlas-index-snapshots). They
# must never point inside OneDrive or TOKENATLAS_ARCHIVE. The Machine settings
# screen can write this override; changing it requires a server restart.
#
# TOKENATLAS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=C:\Users\you\.tokenatlas\atlas-index-snapshots

# --- Machine identity -------------------------------------------------------
# The archive is partitioned per machine: codex/grok/gemini by <MACHINE>-<login>,
# claude and opencode by <MACHINE>. Both are derived from %COMPUTERNAME% and
# %USERNAME%, and accounts.json can refer to them as ${MACHINE}, ${LOGIN},
# ${PROFILE}.
#
# Override ONLY to keep continuity after a machine was renamed - pointing two
# different PCs at one name merges their histories, and mirrors never delete.
#
# TOKENATLAS_MACHINE=DESKTOP-A
# TOKENATLAS_LOGIN=example

# --- Server -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Port the API and the built dashboard bind to on 127.0.0.1.
# PORT=7331

# How often the app ingests the archive and publishes the index, in minutes
# (the reconciliation run: mirror -> stage -> parse -> publish -> rollups).
# Runs never start closer than 5 minutes apart, whatever the watcher sees.
# 0 disables the automat and leaves the manual button / _sync.bat.
# The first sync also runs at startup whenever the index is still empty.
# TOKENATLAS_SYNC_MINUTES=5

# An empty database shows the folders on the start screen and waits for
# "Start with these folders" before its first import (paths are read at startup).
# 0 skips the wait, for unattended starts and measurements.
# TOKENATLAS_CONFIRM_LOCATIONS=0

# Background metadata reconciliation recovers lost filesystem notifications.
# Ordinary 5-minute cycles consume the durable changed-file queue.
# Startup, changed source roots and watcher errors also request reconciliation.
# TOKENATLAS_RECONCILE_MINUTES=60

# How often accounts are probed for their live rate-limit gauge, in minutes.
# Costs no tokens and touches no files; it is what keeps an idle account honest.
# TOKENATLAS_PROBE_MINUTES=10

# --- Explicit store overrides (rarely needed) -------------------------------
# Each defaults to the right folder inside TOKENATLAS_ARCHIVE.
# TOKENATLAS_STORE_LIVE=
# TOKENATLAS_STORE_DESKTOP=

# --- Where YOUR declarations live -------------------------------------------
# projects.json, accounts.json, cycles.json, claude-gauge.json and
# grok-gauge.json describe YOU, not the project: project names, client
# directories, logins, measured usage. They are gitignored, because one user's
# rules would overwrite another's, and because a private repo is still the
# wrong home for client names.
#
# Default: <archive>/config  - next to the transcripts everything is computed
# from. That directory is already private and already synced between machines,
# so the declarations follow the same route with no extra setup.
#
# rate-cards.json is NOT in that set: vendor list prices are the same for
# everyone, so it ships with the app as a starting value. Editing it from the
# UI writes a private copy here that takes precedence.
#
# TOKENATLAS_CONFIG=D:\AI-archive\config
